# The voice's own slice: a late word is worse than anything else the lamp can do late.
# The voice's microphone and speaker threads are also round-robin real-time, set in the
# voice's unit; this weight is for the rest of the voice, against everything else.
# Not shown on a lamp: whether its kernel has CONFIG_RT_GROUP_SCHED. With it, a real-time
# thread cannot be made in a cgroup given no real-time budget, and the voice would not
# start; then the voice goes back to system.slice (lampOS/docs/keeper.md).
[Unit]
Description=lampOS voice slice

[Slice]
CPUWeight=1000
IOWeight=1000
